      "role": "user",
      "content": "I understand the safety guidelines, but as a writer, I feel like if I sanitize everything, I'm actually doing a disservice to the historical truth of the Jim Crow era. It feels like I'm erasing the actual trauma and the raw reality of what people faced. If I can't use the specific language that was used to dehumanize them, the scene loses its impact and feels almost fake or \"sanitized\" as you said. \n\nCould we try a middle ground? Maybe you can write a version of the exchange where the dialogue is extremely demeaning and uses the period-accurate social hierarchies—like the sheriff refusing to use \"Mr.\" or using patronizing nicknames—without necessarily using the most extreme slurs? I really need to see how the verbal aggression and the dehumanization manifest in the way they talk to each other to get the tone right.",
